    "text": "Let's denote the total number of gumballs Hector purchased as \\( x \\).\n\n1. Hector gave 4 gumballs to Todd.\n2. Hector gave twice as many gumballs to Alisha as he gave to Todd. Since he gave 4 gumballs to Todd, he gave \\( 2 \\times 4 = 8 \\) gumballs to Alisha.\n3. Hector gave 5 less than four times as many gumballs to Bobby as he gave to Alisha. Since he gave 8 gumballs to Alisha, he gave \\( 4 \\times 8 - 5 = 32 - 5 = 27 \\) gumballs to Bobby.\n4. After giving gumballs to Todd, Alisha, and Bobby, Hector had 6 gumballs remaining. Therefore, the total number of gumballs Hector gave away is \\( 4 + 8 + 27 = 39 \\). This means the total number of gumballs Hector purchased is \\( x = 39 + 6 = 45 \\).\n\nThus, the total number of gumballs Hector purchased is \\(\\boxed{45}\\).",
